{"id":"u-e26773db-fae7-4d84-bee8-6349704e4ef7","src":"community","title":"Tactical Strength and Fitness","author":"Juan P.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/0KGZ3S-functional-strength-and-overall-fitness","desc":"This program is design to build your whole body as a single unit for overall performance with a form follows function approach. The result is that your body will reflect the fitness level achieved. This program is based on a full body workout focusing on three primary lifts with a couple of accessory exercises. The primary lifts are done as a super set as much as possible with as little rest in between with about 1.5 minutes rest between supersets. Days 2 and 4 focus on overall muscular stamina with mostly bodyweight exercises. The goal is to keep your heart rate up to burn more calories throughout the training session. The RPE increases week to week on the primary lifts for each 4 week wave finishing with a max effort set on week 4. The RPE for the isolation exercises on days 1, 3, and 5 remains the same at 8 - 9.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Bodyweight Fitness","Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-10-12T23:26:09.109Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4","Day 5"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"x":4}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Alternating Dumbbell Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Rolling Tricep Extension (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":4}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Inverted Row","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"use a wide grip to emphasize more upper back engagement"},{"n":"Dip (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Sled Pull/Push","sets":[{"r":2,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"note":"How many reps you do will depend on how much space you have and how much load you put on there. Push down and pull back is one rep. Substitute with farmer's carries or if necessary jump squats."},{"n":"Medicine Ball Throws","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"note":"stand perpendicular about 6 ft from the wall. use a ball with enough weight to make it challenging within the rep range. The rep range is for each side."}]},{"n":"Run","sets":[{"sec":1200,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9}],"note":"Push enough to be uncomfortable but not so much that you die afterwards. If running isn't your thing, substitute with another exercise."}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"x":4}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"JM Press","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":4}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Chin-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Push Up","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"A Skip","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"For about a basketball court length, A skip down and B skip back. Then sprint down and sprint backwards back. Facing the same direction side step down and back. That completes one \"set\"."},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"VO2 Max Intervals","sets":[{"sec":600,"secHi":900,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9}],"note":"I recommend about 2 min. warmup before starting the intervals. I recommend a 30/60 split. 30 seconds hard with a 60 second recovery."}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Zercher Front-Foot Elevated Split Squat","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"Single Arm Dumbbell High Pull","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":